    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d351">

                <pb facs="0582" n="564" sameAs="frus:frus1947v03/pg564"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 EW (Peace)/8–2547: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Representative in Bulgaria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Horner</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sofia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-08-25">August 25,
                        1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>741. Sobranje has just approved unanimously Cabinet decision ratify peace treaty.
                    Foreign Minister Georgiev<anchor n="1" xml:id="d351-f1"/> who was first speaker
                    extolled Soviet Union and said Bulgaria through UN would seek amelioration
                    treaty conditions imposed as result US and UK pressure. Speakers for other
                    parties including opposition then supported ratification. In conclusion
                    provisional president Kolarov<anchor n="2" xml:id="d351-f2"/> reiterated
                    Bulgaria’s intention seeking redress for alleged injustices in treaty especially
                    refusal recognize Bulgaria’s cobelligerency, Bulgaria’s demand for Greek Thrace
                    and reparations clause.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Horner</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d351-f1" n="1" xml:id="d351-f1-content">
                <p>Kimon Georgiev, Bulgarian Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs
                    since November 1946.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d351-f2" n="2" xml:id="d351-f2-content">
                <p>Vasil Petkov Kolarov, Acting President of Bulgaria since 1946.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
